epsy characterized by multiple types of seizures and is treated with the ketogenic diet.", "GUELPA:", "GLUT1:El síndrome de la deficiencia de GLUT1 es un defecto de transporte de glucosa al cerebro que causa epilepsia y retraso en el desarrollo.", "PIRUVATO DESHIDROGENASA:La deficiencia de piruvato deshidrogenasa es un trastorno metabólico que afecta la capacidad del cuerpo para utilizar la glucosa como fuente de energía.", "STATUS EPILEPTICUS:Status epilepticus is a serious medical condition characterized by prolonged or repeated seizures without recovery between them. It is considered a medical emergency due to the potential for significant complications. In cases where status epilepticus is refractory to standard treatments, the ketogenic diet may be utilized as a therapeutic option.", "CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS:CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS, or intensive care, refers to the specialized treatment provided to patients who are critically ill. This care is typically administered in intensive care units (ICUs), which are specialized medical facilities designed to offer comprehensive support to these patients. In ICUs, critically ill individuals receive close monitoring of vital signs, including glucose levels, and nutritional support tailored to their specific needs. Additionally, cuidados intensivos encompasses the management of severe medical conditions, such as status epilepticus, ensuring that patients receive the necessary interventions and therapies to stabilize their health.", "ANTICONVULSIVANTES:Los anticonvulsivantes son medicamentos utilizados para prevenir o tratar las crisis epilépticas.", "CRISIS ATÓNICAS:Las crisis atónicas son episodios de pérdida repentina del tono muscular, lo que puede llevar a caídas o colapsos.", "CRISIS PARCIALES:Las crisis parciales son crisis epilépticas que afectan solo una parte del cerebro y pueden manifestarse de diversas maneras, dependiendo de la región afectada.", "CRISIS TÓNICO-CLÓNICAS GENERALIZADAS:Las crisis tónico-clónicas generalizadas son un tipo de crisis epiléptica que involucra contracciones musculares tónicas seguidas de sacudidas clónicas, afectando todo el cuerpo.", "EPILEPSIA MIOCLÓNICA SEVERA DE LA INFANCIA:La epilepsia mioclónica severa de la infancia es un tipo de epilepsia que se presenta en la infancia y se caracteriza por convulsiones mioclónicas frecuentes y severas.", "ACETAZOLAMIDA:Acetazolamida is a medication that is recommended to be taken on an empty stomach to enhance its absorption. It functions as a carbonic anhydrase inhibitor, which can lead to a significant risk of acidosis if used concurrently with a ketogenic diet.", "ÁCIDO VALPROICO:El ácido valproico es un medicamento que inhibe la β-oxidación y se conjuga con la carnitina acil-transferasa, lo que puede llevar a un déficit de carnitina.", "HIPERAMONIEMIA:La hiperamonemia es una condición médica caracterizada por niveles elevados de amoníaco en la sangre, que puede ser un efecto secundario en algunos pacientes.", "EDEMA CEREBRAL:Edema cerebral, or cerebral edema, is the swelling of the brain caused by an accumulation of excess fluid. This condition can arise in severe cases of hyponatremia and is considered a medical emergency that necessitates immediate intervention. Additionally, cerebral edema can be a complication in patients suffering from various metabolic conditions. The presence of excess fluid in the brain can lead to increased intracranial pressure and potentially serious health consequences, highlighting the importance of prompt diagnosis and treatment."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}